---
epr-meta-version: 1
id: docs-superpowers-default-path-tombstone
covers: subtree
purpose: >
  A tombstone. The top-level docs/ tree was retired on 2026-09-23 and exists only to carry this
  manifest, because the superpowers plugin still saves to docs/superpowers/ by default. Every
  markdown birth here is routed to the governed home, genesis/docs/superpowers/.
rules:
  - id: route-superpowers-default-path
    class: dispatch
    when: { write: "*.md", new: true }
    route-to: { dest: genesis/docs/superpowers/ }
    parameters:
      dispatch-agent: librarian
      dispatch-prompt: >
        Classify the proposed document by kind (design spec, implementation plan, or sprint result)
        and name its governed destination under genesis/docs/superpowers/, or an existing artifact
        it should merge into. Report ROUTE, MERGE, or DROP to the editing agent; do not move or
        create files and do not derail implementation.
    why: >
      docs/superpowers/ is the superpowers plugin's default save path, not this repository's: the
      writing-plans skill saves to docs/superpowers/plans/ and the brainstorming skill to
      docs/superpowers/specs/ unless told otherwise. The governed homes are under
      genesis/docs/superpowers/, chosen by kind. A design spec goes to specs/, born with the
      lifecycle frontmatter that specs/.epr-meta requires. An implementation plan goes to plans/,
      born with id, status and cites. A sprint result or shift journal goes to sprints/. Write the
      file there instead; the placement contract is genesis/docs/PLACEMENT.md.
    retire-when: >
      when every superpowers skill in use saves to genesis/docs/superpowers/ by configuration, so
      nothing is written to the plugin's default path any more
---
# docs/ — tombstone for the plugin default path

This directory holds nothing but this manifest. Specs, plans and sprint results used to land in
`docs/superpowers/{specs,plans,sprint-results}` because that is where the superpowers plugin saves
by default. The repository's design surface is `genesis/docs/superpowers/`, where the lifecycle
gate lives, so a birth here is routed there by kind. The same routing already emptied the legacy
`genesis/docs/plans/` and `genesis/docs/specs/`.

`covers: subtree` is the ownership claim: nothing under `docs/` needs governance of its own,
because nothing is meant to stay here.
